[ti:When Upstream Changes: How Torch Spyre Builds Downstream Confidence]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: Your accelerator backend passed yesterday. Today, PyTorch changes, and something breaks.
[00:00.00]Ava：昨天你的加速器后端还通过了测试。今天 PyTorch 一变，就出问题了。
[00:05.99]How do you catch that early without spending your life sorting through thousands of tests?
[00:05.99]怎样才能及早发现，又不用整天从成千上万个测试里筛查？
[00:12.47]Brian: That's the problem Torch Spyre tackles here.
[00:12.47]Brian：这正是 Torch Spyre 要解决的问题。
[00:15.72]It's the PyTorch backend for the IBM Spyre Accelerator.
[00:15.72]它是 IBM Spyre Accelerator 的 PyTorch 后端。
[00:19.78]The goal is useful feedback when upstream changes, with enough evidence to investigate failures.
[00:19.78]目标是在上游发生变化时提供有用的反馈，并留下足够的证据排查故障。
[00:27.22]Ava: And the starting point is CRCR. Let's unpack that before we collect any more letters.
[00:27.22]Ava：先从 CRCR 说起吧，别急着再加缩写。
[00:34.22]Brian: CRCR means Cross-Repository CI Relay.
[00:34.22]Brian：CRCR 是 Cross-Repository CI Relay，也就是跨仓库持续集成中继。
[00:37.25]CI is continuous integration: automated builds and tests.
[00:37.25]CI 指持续集成，也就是自动构建和测试。
[00:41.93]The relay lets PyTorch trigger testing in downstream repositories and show results to upstream reviewers.
[00:41.93]这个中继让 PyTorch 触发下游仓库的测试，并向上游审查者展示结果。
[00:50.89]Ava: Downstream means a separate project that depends on PyTorch?
[00:50.89]Ava：下游是指依赖 PyTorch 的独立项目？
[00:55.51]Brian: Right. These are out-of-tree backends, maintained outside PyTorch's repository.
[00:55.51]Brian：对。这些后端独立于 PyTorch 仓库，由各自的项目维护。
[01:02.16]CRCR delivers notifications and brings results back to the PyTorch CI CRCR HUD, the shared results dashboard.
[01:02.16]CRCR 负责发送通知，并将结果带回共享的 PyTorch CI CRCR HUD 结果看板。
[01:11.68]Ava: So we've got a delivery service. Who decides what's inside the test package?
[01:11.68]Ava：这么说，配送服务有了。测试包里装什么由谁决定？
[01:17.59]Brian: The backend does.
[01:17.59]Brian：由后端决定。
[01:18.90]CRCR offers four integration levels, and Torch Spyre reached level two, called L2.
[01:18.90]CRCR 提供四个集成级别，Torch Spyre 已达到第二级 L2。
[01:25.20]But choosing meaningful tests and defining what counts as passing remain downstream responsibilities.
[01:25.20]但挑选有意义的测试、定义通过标准，仍是下游项目的责任。
[01:33.30]Ava: Why's choosing tests so complicated?
[01:33.30]Ava：挑测试为什么这么复杂？
[01:35.89]Can't we just test the latest backend against the latest PyTorch?
[01:35.89]直接用最新版后端测试最新版 PyTorch 不行吗？
[01:40.90]Brian: That's the primary combination, together with the latest test suite.
[01:40.90]Brian：这是主要的测试组合，还要配上最新版测试套件。
[01:46.08]There are three moving targets: backend code, PyTorch core, and tests.
[01:46.08]有三个不断变化的部分：后端代码、PyTorch 核心和测试。
[01:51.40]A test change can expose a problem too.
[01:51.40]测试本身的改动也可能暴露问题。
[01:54.72]Ava: Wait, so a new failure doesn't automatically mean the latest PyTorch change caused it?
[01:54.72]Ava：等等，新出现的失败不一定是最新版 PyTorch 的改动造成的？
[02:01.88]Brian: Exactly.
[02:01.88]Brian：没错。
[02:02.49]If only upstream changed since the last passing run, that points toward upstream.
[02:02.49]如果从上次通过测试以来只有上游变了，问题就可能出在上游。
[02:08.66]If several things moved, you need more investigation. Recording the combination matters.
[02:08.66]如果几个部分都变了，就得进一步排查。所以要记录测试时的版本组合。
[02:15.72]Ava: Okay. We know which versions we're testing.
[02:15.72]Ava：好，我们知道要测哪些版本了。
[02:18.78]How do we choose from tens of thousands of tests?
[02:18.78]几万个测试里，该怎么选？
[02:22.62]Brian: They use an agentic pipeline, meaning agents perform the selection work.
[02:22.62]Brian：他们采用智能体流程，由智能体完成筛选。
[02:28.25]It has four stages. First, an agent narrows the search to relevant folders and files.
[02:28.25]流程分四步。第一步，智能体把搜索范围缩小到相关目录和文件。
[02:35.24]Ava: Relevant according to what?
[02:35.24]Ava：相关性怎么判断？
[02:37.60]Brian: The backend's extension points, where it connects to PyTorch, plus plain-language scope preferences.
[02:37.60]Brian：看后端与 PyTorch 对接的扩展点，再结合用自然语言描述的测试范围偏好。
[02:44.36]If automatic differentiation, or autograd, isn't in scope yet, that whole area can be excluded.
[02:44.36]如果自动微分，也就是 autograd，暂时不在范围内，就可以排除整个相关领域。
[02:51.13]Ava: That gets us a smaller library. We still need a way to find the right books.
[02:51.13]Ava：这样书库小了，但还得找到对的书。
[02:56.37]Brian: That's stage two: repository memory.
[02:56.37]Brian：第二步就是建立仓库记忆。
[02:58.93]It builds a searchable index with symbols, files, summaries written by a large language model, and embeddings, numerical representations for finding related tests.
[02:58.93]它建立可搜索的索引，包含符号、文件、大语言模型写的摘要，以及用于查找相关测试的数值表示，也就是嵌入向量。
[03:10.86]Ava: So the next agent doesn't need the entire library squeezed into one prompt.
[03:10.86]Ava：这样下一个智能体就不用把整个书库塞进一条提示词了。
[03:16.25]Brian: Right.
[03:16.25]Brian：对。
[03:16.72]Stage three reads backend code, documentation, and metadata such as supported operators.
[03:16.72]第三步，读取后端代码、文档，以及支持哪些算子等元数据。
[03:23.56]It selects individual tests and classifies them as required to pass or skipped, recording reasons.
[03:23.56]然后逐项选出测试，标记为必须通过或跳过，并记录原因。
[03:31.53]Ava: And stage four checks whether those predictions survive contact with actual hardware?
[03:31.53]Ava：第四步就是上真机，看看这些判断准不准？
[03:37.37]Brian: Exactly. Selected tests run on real hardware.
[03:37.37]Brian：没错。选中的测试会在真实硬件上运行。
[03:41.00]The agent reviews execution logs and revises the classifications.
[03:41.00]智能体查看运行日志，再调整分类。
[03:46.23]Runtime failures and numerical differences can reveal things code analysis missed.
[03:46.23]运行时故障和数值差异，可能揭示代码分析遗漏的问题。
[03:53.18]Ava: That's the part I'd want to review.
[03:53.18]Ava：这部分我会想亲自审核。
[03:55.57]An agent deciding to skip tests could make a dashboard look very peaceful.
[03:55.57]让智能体决定跳过哪些测试，看板可能会显得一片太平。
[04:00.97]Brian: The reasons become comments in the configuration.
[04:00.97]Brian：跳过原因会写成配置文件里的注释。
[04:04.62]The agent proposes; the configuration is the reviewable record.
[04:04.62]智能体提出建议，配置文件留下可供审核的记录。
[04:09.32]The current output covers thousands of individually named test cases.
[04:09.32]目前的输出涵盖数千个逐一命名的测试用例。
[04:14.81]Ava: Let's make that concrete. I've just enabled a new operator. What happens next?
[04:14.81]Ava：举个具体例子。我刚启用了一个新算子，接下来呢？
[04:21.16]Brian: They build a mapping from tests to operators, plus a reverse index from each operator to its tests.
[04:21.16]Brian：他们会建立测试到算子的映射，以及每个算子对应测试的反向索引。
[04:28.23]Think of it as asking which recipes use a newly available ingredient.
[04:28.23]可以把它想成：哪些菜谱会用到一种新食材？
[04:33.51]Ava: But having that ingredient doesn't mean I can cook every recipe.
[04:33.51]Ava：但有了这种食材，不代表每道菜我都能做。
[04:38.61]Brian: Exactly. A test might need other unsupported features.
[04:38.61]Brian：没错。测试可能还依赖其他不支持的功能。
[04:42.83]The selection agent filters those candidates.
[04:42.83]筛选智能体会过滤这些候选测试。
[04:46.34]Operator usage comes from an execution pass using TorchDispatchMode for eager execution and TORCH_LOGS for compiled execution.
[04:46.34]算子使用情况来自一次执行：即时执行用 TorchDispatchMode，编译执行用 TORCH_LOGS。
[04:56.53]Ava: Eager execution runs operations directly. Compiled execution uses compilation.
[04:56.53]Ava：即时执行直接运行操作，编译执行则先经过编译。
[05:02.67]What about updating PyTorch itself?
[05:02.67]那更新 PyTorch 本身呢？
[05:05.78]Brian: They update repository memory and select from newly added or modified tests.
[05:05.78]Brian：他们会更新仓库记忆，并从新增或修改过的测试中筛选。
[05:10.83]Their example upgrade from PyTorch two point thirteen to two point fourteen evaluated about four thousand changed tests.
[05:10.83]他们以 PyTorch 从 2.13 升级到 2.14 为例，评估了约 4000 个变更过的测试。
[05:19.16]Ava: Instead of processing tens of thousands again. That's a smaller review pile.
[05:19.16]Ava：不用再处理几万个测试了，待审的少多了。
[05:24.41]But selected tests might still assume hardware features we don't have.
[05:24.41]但选中的测试仍可能依赖我们没有的硬件功能。
[05:29.59]Brian: That's where declarative configuration comes in: describing the adaptations you want.
[05:29.59]Brian：这就要用声明式配置，写明需要怎样调整。
[05:35.78]They use YAML, a structured text format, to adapt tests without editing upstream test files.
[05:35.78]他们用结构化文本格式 YAML 调整测试，无须修改上游测试文件。
[05:42.83]Ava: For example, a dtype, meaning a tensor's data type, isn't supported?
[05:42.83]Ava：比如不支持某种 dtype，也就是张量的数据类型？
[05:47.98]Brian: You can exclude that dtype while keeping the rest of the test.
[05:47.98]Brian：可以排除这种 dtype，保留测试的其余部分。
[05:52.26]You can also exclude shapes or add dtype coverage.
[05:52.26]也可以排除某些形状，或增加 dtype 覆盖范围。
[05:55.71]One unsupported parameter doesn't have to cost the entire test.
[05:55.71]不支持一个参数，不必放弃整个测试。
[06:00.40]Ava: And the configuration defines which outcomes are acceptable?
[06:00.40]Ava：配置还会规定哪些结果可以接受？
[06:04.79]Brian: Yes.
[06:04.79]Brian：对。
[06:05.12]There are four categories: must pass, expected failure, strict expected failure, and skip.
[06:05.12]有四类：必须通过、预期失败、严格预期失败和跳过。
[06:12.53]With strict expected failure, an unexpected pass is itself reported as a failure.
[06:12.53]严格预期失败的测试如果意外通过，也会被报告为失败。
[06:19.56]Ava: Passing gets me a failure? That's a tough performance review.
[06:19.56]Ava：通过了反而算失败？这考核够严的。
[06:24.01]Brian: It's a useful reminder to promote the test into the must-pass category.
[06:24.01]Brian：这能提醒我们把它升级为“必须通过”的测试。
[06:28.98]There's also an explicit default for unlisted tests, so newly added tests have a defined policy.
[06:28.98]未列出的测试也有明确的默认规则，所以新增测试同样有章可循。
[06:36.05]Ava: How does the framework apply all that without changing the source?
[06:36.05]Ava：框架怎么做到这些，又不改源文件？
[06:40.55]Brian: During test collection, it patches decorators, the helpers that generate test variations.
[06:40.55]Brian：收集测试时，它会给生成测试变体的装饰器打补丁。
[06:47.13]It adds pytest marks, labels used to select tests by operator or dtype.
[06:47.13]它会添加 pytest 标记，用于按算子或 dtype 筛选测试。
[06:52.38]The upstream test tree stays untouched.
[06:52.38]上游测试目录保持原样。
[06:55.62]Ava: Got it.
[06:55.62]Ava：明白了。
[06:56.18]Select tests from evidence, record the reasons, and adapt individual cases through configuration.
[06:56.18]根据证据选测试、记录原因，再通过配置调整具体测试用例。
[07:03.95]Now, when does testing actually start?
[07:03.95]那么，测试什么时候真正开始？
[07:07.34]Brian: A dispatch arrives with information about an upstream pull request, or PR.
[07:07.34]Brian：系统收到一个 dispatch 事件，里面有上游拉取请求，也就是 PR 的信息。
[07:12.91]The workflow checks its action, target branch, labels, and SHA, the identifier for a specific commit.
[07:12.91]工作流会检查操作类型、目标分支、标签和 SHA；SHA 是特定提交的标识。
[07:20.87]Ava: Checking whether a pull request merged sounds straightforward.
[07:20.87]Ava：检查拉取请求是否合并，听起来很简单。
[07:25.25]Brian: There's a wrinkle. PyTorchBot performs the merge and applies a Merged label.
[07:25.25]Brian：这里有个细节：合并由 PyTorchBot 执行，它还会加上 Merged 标签。
[07:31.40]A closed pull request alone isn't enough.
[07:31.40]光是拉取请求已关闭还不够。
[07:34.72]That label can arrive late, and manual merges may omit it.
[07:34.72]这个标签可能延迟出现，手动合并也可能没有它。
[07:39.76]Ava: So critical workflows may need polling or a fallback.
[07:39.76]Ava：所以关键工作流可能需要轮询或备用判断方式。
[07:43.78]What about nightly builds and releases?
[07:43.78]那每夜构建和正式发布呢？
[07:47.09]Brian: Neither gets a CRCR dispatch.
[07:47.09]Brian：两者都不会收到 CRCR dispatch 事件。
[07:49.33]Nightly tests run on a schedule and resolve the source commit.
[07:49.33]每夜测试按计划运行，并确定对应的源代码提交。
[07:54.12]Release tests start manually.
[07:54.12]发布版本的测试则手动启动。
[07:56.36]HUD accepts nightly results but currently lacks a dedicated release view.
[07:56.36]HUD 能接收每夜测试结果，但目前没有专门的发布版本视图。
[08:02.35]Ava: Once testing starts, how do they avoid one enormous job?
[08:02.35]Ava：测试开始后，怎么避免变成一个庞大的任务？
[08:07.47]Brian: They group tests by feature, split groups to meet a duration limit, then balance individual tests using measured timings.
[08:07.47]Brian：他们先按功能分组，再拆分到规定时长内，最后根据实测耗时平衡各测试。
[08:16.38]Thirty minutes is an example limit, not a reported speedup.
[08:16.38]30 分钟只是时长上限的例子，不是报告中的提速数据。
[08:21.07]Ava: And each split builds PyTorch again?
[08:21.07]Ava：每个拆分任务都要重新构建 PyTorch 吗？
[08:24.25]Brian: They build PyTorch and backend wheels, the installable packages, once.
[08:24.25]Brian：他们只构建一次 PyTorch 和后端的 wheel 安装包。
[08:29.43]Every split uses those same artifacts.
[08:29.43]每个拆分任务都使用同一批构建产物。
[08:32.24]That saves repeated builds and keeps the tested software consistent.
[08:32.24]这样既省去重复构建，也保证测试使用的软件一致。
[08:37.61]Ava: What keeps temporary infrastructure trouble from drowning out real regressions?
[08:37.61]Ava：怎样避免临时的基础设施故障掩盖真正的回归问题？
[08:43.07]Brian: Isolated jobs, retries at workflow and job levels, and logs that help classify failures.
[08:43.07]Brian：隔离作业，在工作流和作业层面设置重试，并用日志帮助判断故障类型。
[08:49.95]Non-critical steps can continue after errors.
[08:49.95]非关键步骤出错后可以继续执行。
[08:53.46]The article doesn't provide a complete failure-classification algorithm.
[08:53.46]文章没有给出完整的故障分类算法。
[08:59.43]Ava: There's also a reporting trap with matrix jobs, right?
[08:59.43]Ava：矩阵作业的报告也有个陷阱，对吧？
[09:03.16]Those are jobs generated from combinations of settings.
[09:03.16]矩阵作业是由不同设置组合生成的作业。
[09:07.32]Brian: Yes. Each matrix job has its own check identifier.
[09:07.32]Brian：对。每个矩阵作业都有自己的检查标识符。
[09:11.28]Its in-progress and completed callbacks, the status reports back to CRCR, must come from the same job.
[09:11.28]它向 CRCR 报告状态时，进行中和已完成的回调必须来自同一个作业。
[09:19.72]Ava: What are the options?
[09:19.72]Ava：有哪些办法？
[09:21.75]Brian: Each matrix job can report separately, which may crowd the dashboard.
[09:21.75]Brian：每个矩阵作业可以分别报告，但可能挤满仪表板。
[09:26.68]Or a parent job can dispatch a separate matrix workflow and poll until it finishes.
[09:26.68]也可以由父作业启动单独的矩阵工作流，并轮询直到它结束。
[09:32.97]Ava: And when someone asks what failed two weeks ago?
[09:32.97]Ava：如果有人问两周前哪里出了错呢？
[09:36.89]Brian: Save the dispatch payload, package versions or commits, runtime environment, and individual test results with durations.
[09:36.89]Brian：保存启动参数、软件包版本或提交记录、运行环境，以及每项测试的结果和耗时。
[09:45.47]Keep the build artifacts too.
[09:45.47]构建产物也要保留。
[09:47.54]Those records support reproduction and tracking down the responsible change.
[09:47.54]这些记录有助于复现问题，追查是哪次改动造成的。
[09:53.32]Ava: What's the demonstrated result, and what's still ahead?
[09:53.32]Ava：目前展示了什么成果，接下来还有什么计划？
[09:57.56]Brian: Torch Spyre reached L2 integration.
[09:57.56]Brian：Torch Spyre 已达到 L2 集成。
[10:00.24]The framework targets privateuse1, PyTorch's generic device extension slot.
[10:00.24]该框架面向 privateuse1，也就是 PyTorch 的通用设备扩展槽位。
[10:05.98]They intend to work toward upstreaming reusable parts, with OpenReg, an in-tree reference backend, as a natural reference.
[10:05.98]他们计划推动可复用部分合入上游，并以代码树内的参考后端 OpenReg 作为参照。
[10:15.67]Ava: Three things to remember: CRCR handles coordination and reporting.
[10:15.67]Ava：记住三点：CRCR 负责协调和报告。
[10:20.66]Evidence and reviewable configuration determine meaningful coverage.
[10:20.66]证据和可审查的配置决定了测试覆盖是否有意义。
[10:25.80]Shared artifacts, reliable workflows, and saved metadata make failures easier to investigate.
[10:25.80]共享产物、可靠的工作流和保存的元数据，让故障更容易排查。
[10:33.18]Brian: Thanks for listening, and we'll see you next time.
[10:33.18]Brian：感谢收听，我们下次见。
